  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f9c2d96b525a445ce8f4fb737b923a96, type: 3}
  m_Name: FlyweightUI_Data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Description: 
  m_Title: Flyweight
  m_BodyText:
  - "<b>Flyweight</b> is a design pattern that reduces memory usage that shares data
    across objects instead of duplicating it.\n\nA ScriptableObject can serve as
    a flyweight\u2014a specialized data container that holds shared, immutable data
    accessible to many objects at runtime.\n\nIn this demo, each ball uses a shared
    <b>BallTypeSO</b> ScriptableObject, which defines its visual style and sound\u2014such
    as sprite, and bounce effect."
  - "The BallTypeSO acts as a flyweight: it\u2019s reused across many ball instances,
    separating the presentation from gameplay behavior. \n\nThis keeps memory usage
    low and makes it easy to create style variations\u2014all by updating a single
    asset.\n\nClick the buttons to switch ball types and spawn new balls using different
    flyweight definitions. "
  - "Rather than duplicating data, define it once and reference the flyweight wherever
    it\u2019s needed.\n\nFlyweights work best when many objects share common settings\u2014like
    projectiles, pickups, NPCs, or props. \n\nA bullet hell game might spawn thousands
    of bullets that all use the same shared settings, while a dungeon crawler might
    reuse a single definition for common items found across the level.\n\n"
